[Better Approach 2] Using Bottom-Up DP (Tabulation) - O(n) Time and O(n) SpaceThe idea is to create a1-D array, fill values for first two stairs and compute the values from 2 to n using the previous two results. For i = 2 to n, do dp[i] = cost[i] +  min(dp[i-1] + dp[i-2]). Illustration:
            C++

    // C++ program to count number of
// ways to reach nth stair.
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int minCostClimbingStairs(vector<int> &cost) {
    int n = cost.size();

    if (n==1) return cost[0];

    vector<int> dp(n);
    dp[0] = cost[0];
    dp[1] = cost[1];

    for (int i=2; i<n; i++) {
        dp[i] = cost[i] + min(dp[i-1], dp[i-2]);
    }

    // Return minimum of cost to 
    // climb (n-1)th stair and 
    // cost to reach (n-2)th stair
    return min(dp[n-1], dp[n-2]);
}

